                    <death when="1802"/>
                    <occupation>Philanthroppist, editor</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Samuel Felton died 1802 (PCC wills). Fellow of Royal Society, Fellow of
                            Society of Antiquaries, member of Society for Encouragement of Arts,
                            Manufacture and Commerce. Subscribed 1787 to works of John Jebb, lived
                            at Charlotte St 1786-93, Carburton St 1794-1802. Mentioned in the wills
                            of Timothy Hollis and Thomas Brand Hollis. He wrote some works on art
                            and gardening. May have been the Felton at King's, but obviously not the
                            call of 1815 </p>
                    </note>
